From c50e840fdb30861119253d34d37ccdd6a0af9e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuitianhao <hoopoo@163.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:44:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep OpenStory-bound writing private and synchronized
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

InkOS now selects an isolated project root from the OpenStory-authenticated team, validates signed project bindings before persisting them, and publishes completed screenplay artifacts through a durable HMAC-signed outbox. Studio launch state carries the binding into the persisted session, while generated scripts are normalized into stable chapter sources for OpenStory.\n\nConstraint: InkOS is hosted behind the existing /inkos Nginx path and shares the server with OpenStory.\nRejected: A shared filesystem project with login-only gating | authenticated teams could still read each other’s books, sessions, and artifacts.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: broad\nDirective: Keep port 4567 loopback-only, preserve Nginx identity-header overwrites, and build with INKOS_BASE_PATH=/inkos.\nTested: Studio typecheck; 59 focused tests; client/server builds; cookie-auth tenant isolation; cross-team binding rejection; real script generation and OpenStory sync/outbox retry.\nNot-tested: Full upstream core suite under Bun because existing Zod/pi-agent fixtures fail before these Studio changes.
